# Inert full-worklist permission composition (SOURCE/PURE ONLY)

Based on reviewed PMO7333aad and Finance927ed57. No DB/SQL/native helper/action execution, route, source eligibility, owner policy or public visibility publication. Main/native runtime artifacts untouched.

Registered empty worklists now have a closed witness/context validator in the existing producer. Finance and PMO expose private exact-invocation success consumption: Finance marks its exact binding ticket complete only after final_checked (statement) or exit_checked with no cell (nonstatement), and no pending native denial; the invocation object is registered on that ticket and owned by its reader. PMO consumes its exact complete operation owned by its reader. Neither None nor the last ledger record alone authenticates success. Each succeeds once under current membership/context; stale/mismatched success poisons original/current via reader and producer guards. A new call on the same reader is rejected before further work while its earlier result remains unconsumed. Finance denied-result consumption also unlocks that invocation, retaining all charges. Denied PMO reader remains terminal; a new reader is needed.

compose_permissions takes one exact registered worklist. A marker-global100-attempt limit and exact-worklist processing/complete/failed record survive fresh wrappers. Reentry/replay of the same worklist is forbidden, even after receipt consumption. It freezes all exact Finance row objects followed by all exact PMO row objects. Every row is evaluated once in that sequence, including remaining bindings of already denied templates, both types on one template, and shared runs. It invokes only fixed internal reader classes; no arbitrary callback/plugin. None requires exact reader success consumption; a non-None result must pass that reader's exact one-use denial consumer. There is NO broad PermissionDenied/ValidationError-to-hidden catch. Constructor, malformed, admission, context, cap and SQL failures remain fatal and poison; no partial receipt.

Order within each domain is the deterministic producer PK-order refinement, NOT proven identical to native implicit SQL ordering or first-error ordering. Native Finance PD/VE and PMO PD-only differences are provided by their previously reviewed reader protocols, not reinterpreted here.

Before/after each row and at completion, registered witness/context and operation phase are rechecked. Completion compares exact ordered row identities and lengths, not a count or PK set alone. The frozen repr-suppressed receipt is exact-object registered on its unique attempt and binds witness/worklist/context, completed rows and private denied-template set. No early denied IDs are returned. Private consume_receipt validates exact object/attempt/complete state once and returns None; copied/old receipt misuse poisons original and current markers. Retained byte/cell/domain/query/processing charges never reset/refund. A later domain cap failure after earlier successes is still fatal.

22 new pure definitions cover actual fake registered producer, full order/no denied-template skips, later fatal failure/no receipt, absence of broad native-exception catching, forged/missing success/denial, registered empty and forged inventories, duplicate/replay, tampered completion, context drift, copied/one-use/old receipts, global100 bound; plus actual reader terminal success, pending-before-work rejection, explicit consumed reuse and borrowed invocation/operation negatives. Existing tests were updated to explicitly consume authentic prior results before testing a later invocation, preserving intended underlying phase assertions. 154 composed pure normal/-O PASS. Test stores/readers are stand-ins, NOT SQL/native equivalence proof.

Remaining: all historical claim-template scope restrictions, scope finance document-type gate without claims, exact eligible source predicate and four source-to-hidden-scope relations, full allowed-set/default-prepared equivalence under admission limits, real fixtures/concurrency/rollback. Selected-owner outer gates and engineering caps still narrow admission relative to arbitrary browsing. This receipt attests only complete processing of its private candidate worklist; no full visibility, milestone or production activation claim.
